// `==` between two operands whose type RESOLVES to bare `null` — no `T | null` context on
// either side. DECISIONS.md A-infer-null says an unconstrained `let x = null` resolves to
// the `null` type, so the checker admits this (rc 0) and the emitter owes a lowering; today
// `emitProgram: bare null needs a struct-typed context` (`wasmEmit.vl`, the bare-`null`
// value emitter's fall-through when no struct seed is pending). `const a: P | null = null;
// a == null` RUNS — the ingredient is the ABSENCE of any `T`, not the null itself.
// Found 2026-09-01 by the identity proposal's consistency critique (F10); filed as D1018,
// CLOSED the same day (#2279): the answer is static, no rep needed. Kept as the probe that
// keeps it closed.
// Should print true.
print(null == null)
